  added, add it here: Search Console reports a sitemap that omits a page as
  "discovered but not submitted", which delays indexing.

  lastmod must be a real date. An always-current lastmod trains crawlers to
  ignore the field, so it is updated only when the page actually changes.

  If a custom domain is added, update these URLs and the canonical tags in both
  pages in the same change, or the two will disagree and Search Console will
  report a canonical mismatch.

  URLs include the .html extension because that is the path that exists on
  disk. Extensionless URLs are a host feature, not a file, so a sitemap that
  claims them breaks the moment the site is served from anywhere that does not
  rewrite them. 404.html is deliberately absent: it is noindex and has no
  address of its own.
-->
